    "id": "P62C-CPS-H-026",
    "sourceGame": "micro-concept-library",
    "q": "A firm earns $500 in revenue. Its explicit variable costs are $280 and its explicit fixed lease cost is $70. The owner also forgoes $40 of income from another job. What is accounting profit, and why is the forgone income treated that way?",
    "options": [
      "$110; accounting profit subtracts explicit costs and the $40 forgone income.",
      "$220; accounting profit excludes both the fixed lease and the $40 forgone income.",
      "$190; accounting profit subtracts the lease but adds the $40 forgone income.",
      "$150; accounting profit subtracts explicit costs, so the $40 forgone income is excluded."
    ],
    "tag": "consumer_producer_surplus",
